WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.642
Maggie, and Cole stood on the sidewalk staring at one another.

2
00:00:20.363 --> 00:00:23.706
They'd just proven that Ryan hadn't stolen Maggie's cash.

3
00:00:24.526 --> 00:00:27.029
But they weren't any closer to solving the mystery.

4
00:00:27.049 --> 00:00:32.910
"I guess we should check out some of our other suspects," Henry said to Maggie and Cole.

5
00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:35.512
"What about those two teenage girls?"

6
00:00:35.992 --> 00:00:36.933
Cole suggested.

7
00:00:36.953 --> 00:00:39.896
"They left the scene of the crime pretty fast."

8
00:00:40.737 --> 00:00:41.518
Maggie nodded.

9
00:00:41.538 --> 00:00:48.003
"True. Plus they were whispering together the whole time they were at the lemonade stand, like they were

10
00:00:48.084 --> 00:00:49.245
planning something."

11
00:00:49.265 --> 00:00:53.228
"Do you think they could have taken the money when you weren't looking?"

12
00:00:53.649 --> 00:00:54.509
Henry asked her.

13
00:00:54.529 --> 00:00:56.972
"Sure," Maggie said.

14
00:00:57.792 --> 00:01:01.255
"I had my back to the cashbox while I was talking to Nathan.

15
00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.937
Anyone could have grabbed the money then."

16
00:01:03.957 --> 00:01:09.060
"Okay, let's see if we can track down those girls," Henry said.

17
00:01:10.761 --> 00:01:12.783
They walked back to the lemonade stand.

18
00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:16.425
There was no sign of the two teenagers.

19
00:01:16.445 --> 00:01:20.148
"I think they walked away in this direction," Cole said.

20
00:01:20.708 --> 00:01:21.969
He pointed down the street.

21
00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:25.392
The three of them walked to the end of the block, and then stopped.

22
00:01:26.356 --> 00:01:27.797
"Which way should we go now?"

23
00:01:28.317 --> 00:01:29.098
Maggie wondered.

24
00:01:30.318 --> 00:01:32.379
Henry looked around and spotted Mrs.

25
00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:34.821
Smith watering flowers on her front porch.

26
00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:38.063
She smiled and waved when she saw them.

27
00:01:38.083 --> 00:01:40.164
"Hot day, isn't it?"

28
00:01:40.724 --> 00:01:41.264
she called.

29
00:01:41.284 --> 00:01:45.006
"It sure is," Henry replied politely.

30
00:01:45.026 --> 00:01:51.030
"Mrs. Smith, did you happen to see two teenage girls walk past here recently?"

31
00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:53.591
"Do you mean Jill and Ashley?"

32
00:01:53.951 --> 00:01:54.952
Mrs. Smith nodded.

33
00:01:56.304 --> 00:01:59.825
"Yes, they passed by about ten or fifteen minutes ago.

34
00:02:00.685 --> 00:02:02.086
They were heading toward town."

35
00:02:02.106 --> 00:02:04.686
"Thanks," Henry said.

36
00:02:05.507 --> 00:02:06.727
Then he looked at his friends.

37
00:02:06.747 --> 00:02:08.167
"Come on.

38
00:02:08.607 --> 00:02:09.108
Let's go."

39
00:02:09.948 --> 00:02:13.189
They walked another few blocks until they reached Main Street.

40
00:02:14.009 --> 00:02:17.530
Lots of people were going in and out of the shops and restaurants.

41
00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:21.111
"How are we supposed to find those two girls now?"

42
00:02:21.551 --> 00:02:23.151
Cole asked, looking around.

43
00:02:23.171 --> 00:02:25.172
"They could be anywhere."

44
00:02:26.284 --> 00:02:28.125
"Not really," Henry said.

45
00:02:28.145 --> 00:02:32.287
"I doubt they're in the dry cleaner's or the hardware store.

46
00:02:33.107 --> 00:02:35.728
Teenage girls don't usually go to stores like that."

47
00:02:35.748 --> 00:02:40.070
"True." Maggie was looking around too.

48
00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:45.712
"And it's the middle of the afternoon, so they're probably not at any of the restaurants."

49
00:02:46.712 --> 00:02:49.854
"I bet they're in the drugstore or the bakery," Cole said.

50
00:02:49.874 --> 00:02:55.176
"Maybe we should check the bakery first," he added, licking his lips.

51
00:02:56.684 --> 00:02:57.465
Henry grinned.

52
00:02:58.846 --> 00:03:02.989
He knew that Cole loved the bakery's doughnuts more than almost any other food.

53
00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:05.831
But Henry didn't want to waste any time.

54
00:03:05.851 --> 00:03:09.274
"The drugstore is closer," he pointed out.

55
00:03:10.115 --> 00:03:13.117
"Let's go there first, and then we'll look in the bakery.

56
00:03:13.958 --> 00:03:17.481
If they're not in either place, we could start checking some of the other stores."

57
00:03:18.822 --> 00:03:21.984
The three friends headed across the street to Herman's Drugstore.

58
00:03:22.865 --> 00:03:26.008
As soon as he stepped inside, Henry heard loud giggles.

59
00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:30.723
"Listen! That sounds like them," he whispered to his friends.

60
00:03:31.664 --> 00:03:34.226
He followed the giggling sounds to the makeup aisle.

61
00:03:35.066 --> 00:03:40.530
Jill and Ashley were halfway down the aisle, looking at a display of brightly colored nail polish and

62
00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:41.171
lip gloss.

63
00:03:42.432 --> 00:03:46.835
They didn't notice Henry watching them because they were too busy grabbing stuff from the shelves.

64
00:03:46.855 --> 00:03:53.300
"This is nice," Jill exclaimed, tossing a bottle of sparkly nail polish in a shopping basket.

65
00:03:54.288 --> 00:03:56.110
"It's kind of expensive, isn't it?"

66
00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:57.010
Ashley said.

67
00:03:57.591 --> 00:03:58.392
Then she giggled.

68
00:03:58.412 --> 00:04:00.894
"Oops, never mind.

69
00:04:01.554 --> 00:04:02.955
Who cares if it's expensive?

70
00:04:03.916 --> 00:04:05.497
We have plenty of money!"

71
00:04:05.517 --> 00:04:09.561
"Yeah." Jill giggled and reached for some lip gloss.

72
00:04:09.581 --> 00:04:11.803
"I think I'll buy this too."

73
00:04:12.783 --> 00:04:14.945
Ashley grabbed two more tubes of lip gloss.

74
00:04:14.965 --> 00:04:17.928
"We might as well get a few extras.

75
00:04:18.768 --> 00:04:20.790
After all we can afford it!"

76
00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:25.553
"True," her friend agreed with another loud giggle.

77
00:04:25.573 --> 00:04:29.074
"After we finish here, let's go pick out some candy."

78
00:04:29.094 --> 00:04:32.955
"And then I want to look at the magazines," Ashley said.

79
00:04:33.595 --> 00:04:34.935
Henry's eyes widened.

80
00:04:36.235 --> 00:04:39.816
The teenagers were acting as if they had lots of money to spend!

81
00:04:39.836 --> 00:04:41.497
"I knew it!

82
00:04:42.217 --> 00:04:43.357
Those two did it!"

83
00:04:44.078 --> 00:04:45.438
Maggie said from behind him.

84
00:04:45.458 --> 00:04:47.538
"They stole my money!"

85
00:04:48.439 --> 00:04:49.839
Her voice was kind of loud.

86
00:04:50.639 --> 00:04:53.060
The two older girls heard her and looked over.

87
00:04:54.432 --> 00:04:58.294
"Hey, it's that girl with the lemonade stand," Jill said.

88
00:04:58.314 --> 00:05:02.276
"Shouldn't you be home squeezing lemons or something?"

89
00:05:04.658 --> 00:05:06.899
Ashley started giggling all over again.

90
00:05:07.859 --> 00:05:11.041
Maggie marched over and pointed into their shopping basket.

91
00:05:11.061 --> 00:05:14.002
"Where'd you get the money to buy all that stuff?"

92
00:05:14.603 --> 00:05:15.323
she demanded.

93
00:05:16.724 --> 00:05:18.145
Ashley shot a look at Jill.

94
00:05:19.025 --> 00:05:20.926
Jill frowned and looked down at the floor.

95
00:05:21.787 --> 00:05:23.748
For a second neither of them answered.

96
00:05:24.544 --> 00:05:25.967
Henry traded looks with Cole.

97
00:05:25.987 --> 00:05:33.699
"Is it my imagination," he whispered, "or are those two acting awfully suspicious?"
